# Dependencies
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
yarn.lock

# package-lock.json is COMMITTED on purpose (it was ignored here, which is the
# right call for a published library and the wrong one for a deployed service).
#
# Without it Render resolves every dependency fresh on each build, so the code
# handling payments is not the code that was tested — a transitive package can
# publish a new version between two deploys and change behaviour with no commit
# to point at. It also meant security fixes applied locally never reached
# production, since there was no pinned tree to ship.
#
# frontend/package-lock.json was already tracked; this only aligns the backend.

